---
export const prerender = false;

import HelpLayout from '@/layouts/HelpLayout.astro';
import JsonLd from '@/components/JsonLd.astro';

const siteOrigin = Astro.site?.origin ?? 'https://dreptalk.com';
const pageUrl = `${siteOrigin}/help/voting`;

// FAQ structured data targeting the real searches DReps make about voting on
// DRepTalk. Answers mirror the visible copy below, as Google requires.
const faqLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: [
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'Who can cast a vote on DRepTalk?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'Registered, active, key-credential DReps can vote. Connect a CIP-95 capable wallet (for example Lace, Eternl, or Typhon) and sign in with your DRep key. Script-based DReps are not supported. Reading governance action threads and discussion is public and requires no wallet.',
      },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'How do I vote on a governance action?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'Open the governance action thread and choose Yes, No, or Abstain in the vote panel. You can optionally add a rationale. Click Submit vote and approve in your wallet. DRepTalk is non-custodial: your wallet signs and submits the transaction; the site never touches your keys.',
      },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'Can I edit my vote rationale after submitting?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'No. The rationale is stored as a permanent, content-addressed document and its hash is recorded on chain with your vote. It is shown as a frozen post on the action thread and cannot be edited. If you change your vote while the action is still open, the on-chain vote updates and the rationale post updates to reflect the new vote direction.',
      },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'Can I change my vote after submitting?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'Yes, while the governance action is still open. Open the action thread, choose a different option in the vote panel, and submit. The new vote overwrites the old one on chain. If your previous vote included a rationale, the rationale post on the thread updates to match.',
      },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'What happens to my vote rationale if DRepTalk goes offline?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'Your vote on the blockchain is unaffected. The rationale document is hosted by dreptalk.com, so if the site ever goes away that URL stops resolving. The on-chain hash stays valid forever: anyone can take the same bytes and re-host them at a new URL to restore verifiability. The vote itself needs no rationale URL to remain valid.',
      },
    },
  ],
};

const breadcrumbLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
  itemListElement: [
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'DRepTalk', item: `${siteOrigin}/` },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Help', item: `${siteOrigin}/help` },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: 'Voting', item: pageUrl },
  ],
};
---

<HelpLayout
  title="Voting on governance actions - DRepTalk"
  description="How DReps cast on-chain votes from DRepTalk: who can vote, the optional rationale (permanent and non-editable), re-voting, and the availability tradeoff for hosted rationale documents."
  crumb="Voting"
>
  <JsonLd data={faqLd} />
  <JsonLd data={breadcrumbLd} />

  <p style="color:var(--muted);max-width:62ch;line-height:1.6;">
    DRepTalk lets registered DReps cast on-chain votes directly from a governance
    action thread or from the <a href="/vote">vote dashboard</a>. Voting is
    <strong>non-custodial</strong>: your wallet signs and submits every transaction;
    dreptalk.com never sees your keys. Reading and discussion are always public;
    voting requires a connected DRep wallet.
  </p>

  <section style="margin-top:1.75rem;">
    <h2 style="margin:0 0 0.25rem;font-size:1.0625rem;">Who can vote?</h2>
    <p style="margin:0;max-width:62ch;font-size:0.9375rem;line-height:1.6;color:var(--muted);">
      Only <strong>registered, active, key-credential DReps</strong> can cast
      votes. You need a CIP-95 capable wallet (for example Lace, Eternl, or Typhon)
      and must sign in with your DRep key. Script-based DReps are not supported.
      SPOs, CC members, and direct voters cannot vote here; this flow is for DReps
      only.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-top:1.5rem;">
    <h2 style="margin:0 0 0.25rem;font-size:1.0625rem;">How to vote</h2>
    <p style="margin:0 0 0.5rem;max-width:62ch;font-size:0.9375rem;line-height:1.6;color:var(--muted);">
      Open a governance action thread (or go to <a href="/vote">/vote</a> for the
      full list of open actions) and click the vote panel. Choose
      <strong>Yes</strong>, <strong>No</strong>, or <strong>Abstain</strong>, add
      an optional rationale, and click <strong>Submit vote</strong>. Your wallet
      shows you the transaction details; approve it there. The vote is on chain
      once the transaction confirms.
    </p>
    <p style="margin:0;max-width:62ch;font-size:0.9375rem;line-height:1.6;color:var(--muted);">
      DRepTalk shows an optimistic result immediately so you do not have to wait
      for the next sync. The displayed vote refreshes to the confirmed on-chain
      value within about an hour.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-top:1.5rem;">
    <h2 style="margin:0 0 0.25rem;font-size:1.0625rem;">Vote rationale</h2>
    <p style="margin:0 0 0.5rem;max-width:62ch;font-size:0.9375rem;line-height:1.6;color:var(--muted);">
      Adding a rationale is optional. If you include one, DRepTalk stores it as a
      content-addressed document and records its hash on chain with your vote, making
      the rationale verifiable. The rationale appears as a post on the action thread
      attributed to your DRep.
    </p>
    <p style="margin:0;max-width:62ch;font-size:0.9375rem;line-height:1.6;color:var(--muted);">
      <strong>Rationale posts are permanent and cannot be edited.</strong> The
      on-chain hash fixes the content; any change would produce a different hash and
      invalidate it. If you change your vote (see below), the thread post updates to
      reflect the new vote direction, but the rationale text itself stays as written.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-top:1.5rem;">
    <h2 style="margin:0 0 0.25rem;font-size:1.0625rem;">Changing your vote</h2>
    <p style="margin:0;max-width:62ch;font-size:0.9375rem;line-height:1.6;color:var(--muted);">
      You can re-vote any time while the governance action is still open. Open the
      action thread, select a different option in the vote panel, and submit. The
      new vote overwrites the old one on chain. If you included a rationale with
      your previous vote, the post on the thread updates to show the new vote
      direction alongside the existing rationale text.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-top:1.5rem;">
    <h2 style="margin:0 0 0.25rem;font-size:1.0625rem;">Rationale availability tradeoff</h2>
    <p style="margin:0 0 0.5rem;max-width:62ch;font-size:0.9375rem;line-height:1.6;color:var(--muted);">
      The rationale document is hosted by dreptalk.com. If the site ever goes
      offline, the rationale URL stops resolving. The on-chain hash, however, stays
      valid forever: it commits to the exact bytes of the document. Anyone who has
      those bytes can re-host them at a new URL and anyone else can verify the hash
      matches. Your vote on chain is not affected in any way by the availability of
      the rationale URL.
    </p>
    <p style="margin:0;max-width:62ch;font-size:0.9375rem;line-height:1.6;color:var(--muted);">
      This is the same tradeoff any CIP-100 rationale hosted on a centralized
      service has. The canonical solution is to pin the bytes to IPFS or another
      content-addressed store; that is not built into DRepTalk today, but nothing
      prevents you from doing it yourself and the on-chain hash will still match.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-top:1.5rem;">
    <h2 style="margin:0 0 0.25rem;font-size:1.0625rem;">What voting never does</h2>
    <p style="margin:0;max-width:62ch;font-size:0.9375rem;line-height:1.6;color:var(--muted);">
      Voting never moves your funds beyond the small network fee. DRepTalk never
      asks for a seed phrase or private key. Your wallet shows you the full
      transaction before anything is submitted; if anything looks unexpected,
      reject it.
    </p>
  </section>
</HelpLayout>
